From aa6c95fedb2cfecfb157df75c19ab4f53ea7d370 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:50:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 31/65] Switch Vulkan: GPU frame timeline, on-console GPU
 benchmark, no scene copy

- Timestamps at frame start, scene end, post-processing end and frame end,
  read back without waiting once the frame's fence passed; perf.log
  summaries show GPU ms per frame split into 3D scene, post-processing and
  2D/present, plus handheld/docked mode. The first console logs showed the
  game is GPU bound (CPU 2-4 ms, waiting ~20 ms for the GPU per frame).
- rd_gpubench 1: freezes the level once a map is on screen and measures
  each option (dynamic lights, resolution scale, scene format, ZCULL,
  scene copy) in four directions; results in logs/gpu-bench.txt.
- rd_vk_scenefmt (RGBA16F / RGB10A2 / RGBA8) and rd_vk_zcull now rebuild
  the render buffers on the next frame.
- rd_vk_sceneswap (default on): without MSAA the scene image and
  post-processing image 0 are exchanged instead of blitting the whole
  frame (a full-screen draw on NVK) every frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
